   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: מִי שֶׁהָיוּ יָדָיו צְבוּעוֹת — לֹא יִשָּׂא אֶת כַּפָּיו. תָּנָא: אִם רוֹב אַנְשֵׁי הָעִיר מְלַאכְתָּן בְּכָךְ — מוּתָּר.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna that «Rabbi Yehuda said: One whose hands are colored should not lift his hands» to recite the Priestly Benediction. It was «taught» in a baraita: «If most of the townspeople are engaged in this occupation,» dyeing, «he is permitted» to recite the Priestly Benediction, as the congregation will not pay attention to his stained hands."
  }
